From 4cda58e197b29a292a0b98c1f3366f90ef4d986c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nsbradley88 <3960699+nsbradley88@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 09:39:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 35/46] vulkan: decode lightning indexer for small batches
 (GLM-5.3-Flash DSA)

The tiled indexer shader stages 64 keys x 8 tokens per workgroup and walks the 32 heads
with a barrier per head, so at 1-3 tokens most invocations idle and each workgroup runs a
long serial loop: 0.43 ms per call at 32K context (8K pooled keys), 0.75 ms at 64K.

lightning_indexer_vec.comp handles batches of up to 8 tokens (GGML_VK_LID_VEC_MAX_TOKENS,
0 = off): one invocation per key holds the key row in registers and scores it against
every head, q and the head weights are workgroup-uniform loads, one workgroup per 64 keys
and token. Everything is fp32 (the tiled shader rounds q and k to f16).

test-backend-ops perf, Radeon 8060S, 32 heads x 128, f32 keys (old -> new):
  2K keys  n=1 119 -> 12.7 us, n=3 122 -> 14.8 us
  8K keys  n=1 430 -> 17.9 us, n=3 432 -> 30.6 us
  16K keys n=1 747 -> 24.0 us, n=3 754 -> 58.1 us

test-backend-ops: decode-sized indexer cases (odd head counts, ragged key counts, two
streams, f32/f16/bf16/q8_0/q4_0) and GLM-shaped eval and perf cases.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
